===== verify:ext_features:leakage.json
{
 "agentId": "a8b1339a7713e3bb6",
 "label": "verify:ext_features:leakage",
 "phase": "Verify",
 "result": {
  "refuted": false,
  "severity": "minor",
  "issues": [
   {
    "what": "Descriptive statistics in the fit reports and FINDINGS were computed over OOS bars and OOS SETUP rows (label-free, choose nothing): per-column coverage over all 5326 / 1012 rows (824 / 180 of them OOS), BOCPD MAP-reset rates and CUSUM event totals over the whole tape divided by all 1188 sessions (162 OOS), HMM/GMM/jump state_share_tape over all bars, tape_forward_loglik over all bars.",
    "where": "research/strategy_lab/fz_v3/out/studies/ext_features/build_ext.py lines 114, 138, 182, 208-209, 267; write_docs.py line 75; FINDINGS.md coverage table and 'Columns below 0.95 coverage' line",
    "evidence": "build_ext.py:138 `np.sum(np.diff(m_) < 0)) / len(S)` with m_ over all n bars and S = every session; :267 `X[c_].notna().mean()` over the full SETUP table; data/<tf>/features.parquet split counts reproduced as IS 4502 / OOS 824 (minute), IS 832 / OOS 180 (5minute). No label column is read anywhere (build_ext reads bars, events, sessions and three as-of feature columns; write_docs reads only harness.load(tf).n), and no fitted quantity depends on these aggregates (fit_mask = IS & 2021-10-01..2023-09-30, recomputed 182557 / 36514 bars, 489 sessions, last fit bar dated 2023-09-29).",
    "fix": "Recompute coverage, reset rates, event totals, state shares and the tape log-likelihood on IS rows / IS bars only (or label the reported numbers as whole-tape aggregates) so the study's own claim 'the only label-side read is the row count' extends to 'no OOS row or bar entered any reported statistic'."
   },
   {
    "what": "Both judges made the HMM (and Judge 2 the jump model) conditional and the study ran them unconditionally on both timeframes: Judge 1 'run the HMM only if study 3 shows the H2 counts are not already the regime cluster, and then on 5m only'; Judge 2 'fit the HMM/jump model only if the GMM state already shows a kept-vs-skipped signal at matched skip fraction versus n_choch_since_bos on CV'. Because no ledger trial was run, the only consequence is 19 extra candidate columns per timeframe (hmm{3,4}_* 15, jump{3,4}_* 4) entering the importance study's vocabulary; this is a multiplicity cost that must be counted there, not a leakage.",
    "where": "research/strategy_lab/fz_v3/DESIGN_PANEL.md lines 102 and 104 (the two fixes) vs research/strategy_lab/fz_v3/out/studies/ext_features/build_ext.py lines 186-242 (HMM K3/K4 and jump K3/K4 on both `--tf minute` and `--tf 5minute`, no condition)",
    "evidence": "build_minute.log lines 'HMM K=3 fitted', 'HMM K=4 fitted', 'jump model K=3/4' on the 1-minute tape; ledger/trials.jsonl contains 0 rows mentioning ext_features or features_ext (888 rows total), so no gate was searched on them. FINDINGS.md does not record the departure from the judges' condition.",
    "fix": "Record the deviation in FINDINGS.md / findings.json caveats (the judges' condition was not checked before fitting), and have the importance study count the hmm*/jump* columns in its trial family; alternatively withhold the 1-minute hmm*/jump* columns until the GMM-vs-n_choch_since_bos condition has been evaluated through harness.score."
   },
   {
    "what": "d* for the FFD of log close was chosen on the fit window (0.2) although the design defines d* as the smallest d whose ADF passes on IS bars; on all IS bars d = 0.2 fails the ADF at 5% and only 0.3 passes, so the shipped ffd_close_dstar column is non-stationary by the design's own IS-wide criterion. Label-free, documented as a caveat, not a leakage.",
    "where": "research/strategy_lab/fz_v3/DESIGN_PANEL.md line 244 ('d* = smallest d whose ADF statistic on IS bars is below the critical value') vs research/strategy_lab/fz_v3/out/studies/ext_features/build_ext.py line 93 (`d_star = d_fit`)",
    "evidence": "Reproduced on 5minute with statsmodels adfuller (constant, 2 lags): d=0.2 fit window stat -5.246 (pass), all IS stat -2.543 vs crit -2.862 (fail); d=0.3 all IS stat -4.686 (pass). The report's d_star_fit 0.2 / d_star_is 0.3 for close on both timeframes match.",
    "fix": "Either add a second column at the IS-wide d* (0.3) so the importance study can compare, or state in the handover that the FFD column is at d = 0.2 and is not stationary over all IS by the ADF rule the design specified."
   }
  ],
  "verified": "Read STUDY_AGENT_BRIEF.md, OUT/README.md, data/README.md, BRIEF.md, DESIGN_PANEL.md (regime-states, rocket-probe, vision-labels, motif-shapelet, feature-importance, regime-breaks sections with both judges' fixes), FINDINGS.md, findings.json, features_ext/README.md, build_ext.py, ext_lib.py, finalize.py, write_docs.py, run_minute.sh, all six logs, and harness.py (load / asof_columns / OOS guard). No study, ledger or data file was modified (ext_lib.py was copied to the scratchpad for the checks; the study folder has no __pycache__). Reproduced independently: (1) shapes 5326x62 / 1012x62 full, 3807x62 / 718x62 truncated, ext_features.parquet identical to ext_features_all.parquet (61 feature columns, none with a forbidden prefix, none duplicating a base as-of column), setup_i equal to the base table's; (2) the truncation diff on the truncated builds themselves: trunc ext_fit_report.json `data` = .../data/<tf>/trunc_20250630_120000, bars 335934 / 67192, the truncated bars.parquet is the exact prefix of the full tape ending 2025-06-30 12:00:00, SETUP keys before the cut identical (3807 / 718), max |diff| 0.0 and 0 NaN-pattern mismatches across all 61 columns on both timeframes, fitted quantities identical (d*, state means, lambda*, BOCPD and z-scoring statistics; logs of the trunc builds show identical EM iterations and filter-validation numbers); (3) the fit window: is_mask & date in [2021-10-01, 2023-09-30] gives 182557 / 36514 bars over 489 sessions, last fit bar dated 2023-09-29, next bar 2023-10-03, well before the cut; IS has 1026 
